upsc.append({"q":"According to Goh Cheng Leong, petroleum typically accumulates in which of the following geological settings?","o":["Dome-shaped anticlines between two layers of non-porous rock, oil traps formed by faults, or pools capped by an impermeable volcanic dyke","Only in flat sedimentary basins with no folding or faulting whatsoever","Exclusively within metamorphic rock formations under extreme heat and pressure","Only at the base of extinct volcanoes, mixed directly with lava flows"],"a":0,"e":"The text explicitly describes three oil-trapping settings: dome-shaped anticlines (oil at the crest, gas above, water below), fault-created traps where porous and non-porous strata are juxtaposed, and traps capped by an impermeable volcanic dyke — not flat unfolded basins, metamorphic rock, or lava-mixed deposits."})

upsc.append({"q":"Which one of the following statements about the modern oil industry, per Goh Cheng Leong, is NOT correct?","o":["The modern oil industry began with early 'wild-catting' random drilling, a practice that remains the standard, most cost-effective method used by oil companies today","The modern oil industry began in 1859 when Edwin Laurentine Drake sunk the first oil well in Titusville, Pennsylvania","Modern oil prospecting is highly technical, involving geological surveys and instruments to detect rock density, permeability and structure before drilling","Modern oil wells can be sunk to depths between a few hundred metres and 6,700 metres, at costs that can run into millions"],"a":0,"e":"This statement is incorrect and reverses the actual account — the text explicitly states that early random 'wild-catting' has been replaced by a highly technical, scientific process using precise instruments, since blind drilling at modern costs would be a 'terrific waste of money'; wild-catting is not the modern standard. The other three statements are correct."})

upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about world petroleum production and refining, per Goh Cheng Leong:\n1. About 60% of the world's oil reserves are estimated to lie in the Middle East.\n2. Pipelines are the cheapest and most efficient method of transporting crude oil overland for great distances.\n3. Oil refineries located in or near the oilfields are generally the largest and most economical, since transport costs to the refinery are eliminated entirely.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect — the text explicitly describes refineries located in or near oilfields as only a TEMPORARY measure applying to small refineries (since oilfields are often remote with little industrial demand), not the largest or most economical option; the largest, internationally-owned refineries are instead at ports of import. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

