upsc.append({"q":"Which one of the following statements about hydro-electric power (H.E.P.), per Goh Cheng Leong, is NOT correct?","o":["Over two-thirds of the world's electricity supply comes from hydro-electric plants, with thermal power contributing only a minor share","Regions with the greatest H.E.P. development have strong relief, such as Scandinavia, Alpine Europe, Canada, the U.S.A. and Japan","Norway, lacking both coal and oil, has fully developed its water-power resources and has the highest per capita output of water power in the world","H.E.P. requires a steep gradient, a sufficient and constant volume of water, heavy capital outlay, and a large domestic/industrial market"],"a":0,"e":"This statement is incorrect and reverses the actual proportion — the text explicitly states over two-thirds of the world's electricity comes from THERMAL plants, with hydro-electric power making up only about a third of the world's electricity supply, not the reverse. The other three statements are correct."})

upsc.append({"q":"Match List-I (Dam/Scheme) with List-II (Location or Purpose, per Goh Cheng Leong) and select the correct answer using the code below.\nList-I:\nA. Grand Coulee Dam\nB. Hoover (Boulder) Dam\nC. Kitimat Scheme\nD. Tennessee Valley Authority (T.V.A.)\nList-II:\n1. Supplies H.E.P. for aluminium smelting in British Columbia using imported Jamaican bauxite\n2. World's highest dam, controlling the Colorado River and supplying Los Angeles/San Francisco\n3. Over 30 multi-purpose dams rehabilitating a devastated area since 1933\n4. World's largest concrete dam, in Washington state\nCodes:","o":["A-4, B-2, C-1, D-3","A-2, B-4, C-1, D-3","A-4, B-2, C-3, D-1","A-4, B-1, C-2, D-3"],"a":0,"e":"The correct match is A-4, B-2, C-1, D-3: the Grand Coulee Dam is the world's largest concrete dam; the Hoover Dam is the world's highest, controlling the Colorado River; the Kitimat Scheme supplies H.E.P. for aluminium smelting using Jamaican bauxite; and the T.V.A. rehabilitated a devastated region through over 30 multi-purpose dams."})

upsc.append({"q":"Assertion (A): Countries like Norway, Sweden, Canada and Japan, despite being deficient in mineral fuels, have attained a high level of industrial development.\nReason (R): These countries developed cheap hydro-electric power ('white coal'), which supports energy-intensive industries such as aluminium smelting and the production of nitrates and calcium carbides.\nWhich one of the following is correct in respect of the above Assertion (A) and Reason (R)?","o":["Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true, but R is NOT the correct explanation of A","A is true, but R is false","A is false, but R is true"],"a":0,"e":"Both are true and R explains A — Goh Cheng Leong explicitly attributes the industrial success of these mineral-fuel-poor nations to their development of cheap H.E.P. ('white coal'), which specifically enables electro-chemical industries like aluminium smelting, nitrate and calcium carbide production."})

