upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about nuclear and non-conventional energy in India, per NCERT — entirely new content not found in Goh Cheng Leong:\n1. India's Atomic Energy Institute at Trombay, established in 1954, was later renamed the Bhabha Atomic Research Centre in 1967.\n2. Thorium in India is mainly obtained from monazite and ilmenite in beach sands along the coasts of Kerala and Tamil Nadu.\n3. India's largest wind power plant, located at Lamba in Kachchh, Gujarat, is also the largest in Asia.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1, 2 and 3","1 and 2 only","2 and 3 only","1 and 3 only"],"a":0,"e":"All three statements are correct, matching NCERT's account of the Trombay-to-BARC renaming, thorium's monazite/ilmenite beach-sand sources in Kerala/Tamil Nadu, and the Lamba (Kachchh, Gujarat) wind farm's status as the largest in Asia."})

